+## Implementation Notes for phase3-dx (Dev1) — 2026-06-08 (this subagent worktree)
+
+**Assigned task**: phase3-dx — Make `python -m pytest` from repo root reliably work after `pip install -e .[dev]` (and even before) on Windows pwsh/cmd/bash without requiring manual $env:PYTHONPATH='src' or equivalent.
+
+**Approach chosen (minimal + robust, exactly as suggested in plan + task)**:
+- Added a new `tests/conftest.py` (no prior conftest existed in root or tests/).
+- The guard is a stdlib-only module-level try/except at import time:
+  ```python
+  try:
+      import crap4code
+  except ImportError:
+      _src_dir = ...computed from Path(__file__).parent.parent / "src"...
+      if _src_dir.is_dir() and ... not in sys.path:
+          sys.path.insert(0, str(_src_dir))
+  ```
+- Only prepends when the package is *not* importable as installed (or via pytest's pythonpath bootstrap). This is the safe "if not importable as installed" pattern requested.
+- Kept the existing `pythonpath = ["src"]` + `testpaths` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` in pyproject.toml (it still aids pytest collection; the guard is belt-and-suspenders).
+- Enhanced the pyproject pytest section with explanatory comments (no behavior change).
+- Updated README.md "Development" section with explicit cross-shell "just works" examples using `&&` (works in pwsh/cmd/bash), plus a full subsection explaining the historical friction, the guard mechanism, "before" and "after" support, Teach-Through-Code reference to the conftest docstring, and note that CI already follows the pattern.
+- Updated AGENTS.md (Primary Commands + new note) for consistency (prevents doc drift for agent users).
+- Followed "Teach Through Code" + structured doc: rich module docstring on conftest.py (purpose, root cause, chosen fix, verification, how it fits the lazy registry / python-only sims, no-prod-impact), targeted inline comments, absolute-path derivation for robustness.
+- No production code touched whatsoever. No new runtime (or even test) dependencies.
+- The lazy registry (D1) is explicitly called out as compatible (top-level import now succeeds for python even in grammar-mocked sims; the guard makes the package reachable for test collection in those scenarios too).
+
+**Why this approach (vs alternatives)**:
+- Pure pytest config tweaks or pytest-srcpaths plugin rejected (prefer no extra dep, and config alone was the historical source of the friction per the plan's Dev1 description).
+- Unconditional sys.path prepend avoided (would mask installed vs src differences and violate the "only if not importable" spec).
+- Root-level conftest vs tests/conftest: tests/ location is standard, still loaded early enough by pytest for the test modules' imports, and keeps test-only concerns together.
+- Editable install + `python -m pytest` recommended as primary (matches CI, AGENTS, release-checklist, existing README), with the guard making the "even before" and "no-env-var" cases first-class.
+- Matches the exact suggestions in the plan under Dev1 and the user task description.
